and similar variants in the code (uhitm.c specifically)...  the only
one that isn't like that is this from weapon.c:

if (ptr == &mons[PM_SHADE] && objects[otyp].oc_material != SILVER)
    tmp = 0;

Meaning tmp isn't set to 0 only when you hit a shade with a silver
object.  It was during this study I also found that 2 silver rings,
when attacking a silver-hating monster barehanded and w/o gloves, is
no better than one:

if (!uarmg) {
    if (uleft && objects[uleft->otyp].oc_material == SILVER)
        barehand_silver_rings++;
    if (uright && objects[uright->otyp].oc_material == SILVER)
        barehand_silver_rings++;
    if (barehand_silver_rings && hates_silver(mdat)) {
        tmp += rnd(20);
